<p>Anthropic has told the US government it will not give the Pentagon “unconditional” access to its AI models. The company says it can’t accept terms that would allow uses it considers unethical, including mass surveillance and systems that could enable fully autonomous weapons. The dispute is spotlighting a growing tension: militaries want to deploy commercial AI at scale, while private firms try to set clear red lines for national-security work.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TRxiV-zKtxEH5QdvNlKEROUl-Ida0O0bflE9Yobt9fM78jovpmY450Ybgjx_n9jvm24PnHlq79zuRtkBm-zfdlJoQXedBdGx4DB13hOzYaerWcsqvjA1e7S2pJubzr_Vgs9HbO3bEPr-DJJwr2qNLtgBBO9JnPOi-GeeISnIYDFjp4yVbLh2IR_TdV3u_FCFS1xZXeM57Q0eRnK27d6tkC0ERzcpL51zAhBriOB0zssB2LwuMmMTFRwe7uFzeXspG0Op4p0HQcMgyTvpDg' alt='Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei at the AI Impact Summit in New Delhi, Feb. 19, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Broader procurement stakes: US officials warned they could cancel Anthropic’s existing government agreements—not just a single Pentagon contract—if the company doesn’t reach a Defense Department deal.</li><li>Backstop of compulsion: Some coverage says officials have discussed using federal emergency powers or Cold War-era authorities to compel cooperation if negotiations break down.</li><li>Guardrails focus: Anthropic casts the fight as pressure to drop or weaken model “guardrails,” not as a blanket refusal to work with the defense establishment.</li><li>Democracy concerns: Anthropic argues that unrestricted military use of its systems could erode democratic norms, especially if it enables surveillance and other domestic-facing applications.</li><li>Concrete mission examples: Commentary has pointed to past or hypothetical operational scenarios—such as discussion of a mission to capture Venezuelan leader Nicolas Maduro—to show the kinds of military uses that raise ethical questions for commercial AI vendors.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Anthropic (Dario Amodei): The CEO says the company “cannot in good conscience” accept the government’s terms for unconditional use. He cites red lines that include mass surveillance (including of US citizens) and fully autonomous weapons. (<a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/technology/science/article-anthropic-ceo-pentagon-military-mass-surveillance-weapons-pete-hegseth/'>The Globe and Mail</a>, <a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/anthropic-says-wont-give-us-military-unconditional-ai-use'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>US Defense Department: Reporting says Pentagon officials pushed Anthropic to loosen guardrails; one account describes a senior defense official posing a battlefield hypothetical to test the company’s safety-first stance. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-26-0800/defense-and-security-anthropics-pentagon-showdown-about-more-ai-guardrails'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>US government (contracting stance): US officials warned they would end Anthropic agreements without a Pentagon deal, signaling they’re willing to use procurement leverage in the negotiations. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/11d27612-d6c5-4cf7-94dd-f65603549b7f'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Le Monde (reported US stance): Le Monde reports the government has threatened to force compliance using federal emergency powers if Anthropic does not provide unrestricted access. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/27/anthropoic-says-it-will-not-give-us-government-unrestricted-use-of-ai_6750909_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-02-26-0800/defense-and-security-anthropics-ethics-rules-tests-americas-big-tech-and-military-partnership'>Anthropic&#x27;s ethics rules tests America&#x27;s Big Tech and military partnership</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/technology/science/article-anthropic-ceo-pentagon-military-mass-surveillance-weapons-pete-hegseth/'>Anthropic CEO says AI company cannot accept Pentagon’s demands ‘in good conscience’</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/ai-firm-anthropic-rejects-unrestricted-us-military-use/a-76143608'>AI firm Anthropic rejects unrestricted US military use</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/anthropic-says-wont-give-us-military-unconditional-ai-use'>Anthropic says it won’t give US military unconditional AI use</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/02/27/anthropoic-says-it-will-not-give-us-government-unrestricted-use-of-ai_6750909_4.html'>Anthropic says it will not give US government unrestricted use of AI</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/11d27612-d6c5-4cf7-94dd-f65603549b7f'>US warns it will axe all Anthropic agreements without Pentagon deal</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/anthropic-says-wont-give-us-military-unconditional-ai-use/article70682418.ece'>Anthropic says won&#x27;t give U.S. military unconditional AI use</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>